<title>UK: GERMAN INLAND GAS OIL MARKED HIGHER, DOLLAR STEADY.</title>
<headline>GERMAN INLAND GAS OIL MARKED HIGHER, DOLLAR STEADY.</headline>
<text>
<p>(DLR/DM=1.8641)   DM/100 LTRS     DLRS/100 LTRS   LAST DM</p>
<p> HAMBURG	     35.70/36.10     19.15/19.36   35.30/35.70</p>
<p> BREMEN		35.70/36.10     19.15/19.36   35.30/35.70</p>
<p> DUISBURG	    35.80/36.20     19.20/19.41   35.40/35.80</p>
<p> FRANKFURT	   36.40/36.80     19.52/19.74   36.00/36.40</p>
<p> KARLSRUHE	   36.50/36.90     19.58/19.79   36.10/36.50</p>
<p> INGOLSTADT	  37.40/37.80     20.06/20.27   37.00/37.40</p>
<p>German inland gas oil prices were marked up around 30 to 40 pfennigs on Tuesday, reflecting firmer London futures values. Traded volume was at the low levels normally seen in summer. The dollar was steady. -- London newsroom, +44 171 542 7646</p>
</text>
